BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre": "https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/09/28th-annual-family-friends-golf-tournament"}
X-SOURCE-ID:jccc
SUMMARY:The 28th Annual Family & Friends Golf Tournament
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T200000
UID:66dcf7ffbdfc04fc8c0c3fec95ab74f8@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Golf Registration is Closed! ⛳ Thank you for the incredible 
 support! The 28th Annual Family & Friends Golf Tournament will be held on 
 Sunday September 13\, 2026\, on the Classic Course at Rolling Hills Golf C
 lub in Stouffville. This day is also National Grandparents’ Day\, so we 
 will have special prizes for the Grandparent/Grandchild Champions! This is
  a chance for families and friends to share a fun day of golf – all skil
 l levels are welcome and there are lots of prizes to be won! After a great
  day of golfing\, there will be games\, a raffle\, prize presentations and
  dinner back at the JCCC. We encourage everyone to join with grandparents\
 , grandchildren\, parents\, siblings\, aunts\, uncles\, cousins\, or just 
 as a group of friends. There will be awards for 3 categories: iA Private W
 ealth Cup (Lowest Scramble Score for foursome) Consul General Cup (Lowest 
 Family* Scramble) * Must all be related Roy & Kay Shin Memorial Cup (Lowes
 t Grandparent/Grandchild Score) Note: a foursome cannot win more than 1 ca
 tegory. As in the past\, it will be an early Shotgun format (8:30am start 
 for everyone) and the format is a Texas Scramble (where everyone hits a te
 e shot\, then the foursome picks the best lie\, and everyone else plays th
 eir ball from that spot\, and so on). We are so appreciative of iA Private
  Wealth's Marty Kobayashi\, confirmed again this year as our Platinum Spon
 sor. So please come on out for a fun day!! The Tournament is limited to th
 e first 144 golfers registered. We had an overwhelming response last year 
 so make sure to get your registration submitted before it fills up. REGIST
 RATION NEW THIS YEAR: Registration will ONLY be on-line through the "Regis
 ter" link below. You must register the whole team (4 players) at sign up. 
 See below for the details. The registration link will open on Monday July 
 13\, 2026 at 10 AM . Please note that Green Fees\, Cart Rental fees and fo
 od prices have all gone up substantially over the past year\, so we have n
 o choice but to increase entry fees. However\, we have eliminated the 2-pr
 ice system so now all golfers pay the same price: Entry Fee: Regular 4 pla
 yer team ($145 pp - includes tax) OR Gold Sponsor 4 player team $680. Fees
  include – Green fees/Shared Power Cart/Musubi Lunch/Awards/Dinner/Prize
 s. Dinners only: Adults $35 (includes tax) / Children (under 10 years $12 
 (includes tax)). More Registration details: Register as 4 person Teams –
  Regular Fee or as Gold Sponsor Register up to 2 teams in one application.
  Award categories and extra dinners are included in the registration form.
  Main contact/payee required to sign up by name\, additional players can b
 e left anonymous. Substitute players allowed\, no refunds. Contact the org
 anizers to confirm all player names no later than Monday August 31st . Oth
 er sponsorship types: In Memoriam ($200) / Bronze level ($200) which inclu
 de signage and 2 adults dinners – please contact the organizers to provi
 de more details. Register *Player registration is full. Dinner\, and In Me
 moriam and/or Bronze sponsorship are still available until August 14. For 
 ALL inquiries/questions : Organizers Sharon Marubashi by e-mail \, or cell
  (647-291-4751) and Dawna Kobayashi by e-mail \, or cell (416-407-8102).\n
 \nCategories: Community Event
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/09/28th-annual-family-friends-golf-tourn
 ament
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
