SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T143000
UID:6a909bf6b204780029960889@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse\nA class on how to us
 e a mouse for absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nI
 n this first session you will:\nObserve and practice how to operate a mous
 e effectively\nUnderstand various mouse pointers and cursors\nReview basic
  keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for basic Windows functions\nUpon compl
 etion of this class students will be able to use a computer mouse at a bas
 ic level and will be able to go online for additional practice.
LOCATION:Black Creek
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a909bf6b204780029960889
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a516f350d65ac36003eded2"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Creative Writing For Newcomers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T143000
UID:6a516f350d65ac36003eded2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program provides a supportive\, low-pressure environment 
 where newcomers can build confidence in their English writing\, communicat
 ion\, and presentation skills. Together\, we will:\n1. Have a short\, coll
 ective discussion period.\n2. Begin writing based on a prompt from the ins
 tructor\n(Example: This year\, I learned... Last week\, I did... Something
  funny happened when…)\n3. Present what we wrote to the group.\nPlease n
 ote: This is a group meeting. We do not offer individual lessons. We will 
 not be spell-checking\, looking at punctuation\, grammar\, ect. We will be
  focusing on basic sentence structure and presentation.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (Youth Hub\, First Floo
 r)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a516f350d65ac36003eded2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
