BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ben McNally Books": "https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ben_mcnally_bm
SUMMARY:Reclaiming Canadian Sovereignty Book Launch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T190000
UID:bm-6313420260914@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/2026_09_14.png?cb=1788895784
DESCRIPTION:[at Ben McNally Books]\nJoin us at Ben McNally Books\, in part
 nership with James Lorimer Books\, to celebrate the launch of\nReclaiming 
 Canadian Sovereignty in a Ruptured World\n\, edited by Bob Rae.\nOrder a
  copy of\nReclaiming Canadian Sovereignty\nhere.\nAbout the Book\nIn this 
 timely book about Canada in a changing world\, former Canadian ambassador 
 to the United Nations Bob Rae brings together twenty of Canada’s leading
  voices to address urgent questions about Canadian sovereignty\, at home a
 nd internationally.\nAs our relationship with the United States becomes in
 creasingly unpredictable\, questions of Canada’s future have never been 
 more pressing. Prominent Canadians from the worlds of journalism\, governm
 ent\, the arts and academia weigh in on the key issues facing our country 
 today. What does the “ruptured” global order mean for Canada at home a
 nd abroad?\nOn trade and industry\, the climate crisis\, global alliances 
 and defence\, and political and cultural policy\, leading figures from acr
 oss the country propose what Canadians need to do to strengthen and safegu
 ard our sovereignty.\nWith contributions from Margaret Atwood\, Lloyd Axwo
 rthy\, Michael Kovrig\, and more.
LOCATION:Ben McNally Books
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2d79061e67cd9cb339aa3d"}
