UID:9aan30u1bmtu0i2o8ci2ngkluk@google.com
CREATED:20260729T133245Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Title: <b>CHIME and the Transient Radio Sky</b></p>\n\n<p>Ab
 stract: The Canadian Hydrogen Intensity Mapping Experiment is an excellent 
 instrument for studying\nthe variable radio sky\, particularly Fast Radio B
 ursts and radio pulsars\, including the new class of \nLong-Period Radio Tr
 ansients.  I will describe the CHIME/FRB instrument and its Outrigger teles
 copes and present the latest results on FRBs.  Additionally\, I will report
  on recent discoveries of LPTs and an ongoing new and unusual search for Ga
 lactic radio pulsars.  Finally\, I will describe\nplans for a major upgrade
  of CHIME/FRB designed to unveil the microsecond sky.</p>\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T154216Z
LOCATION:MP1318A
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Victoria Kaspi (McGill University)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
