SUMMARY:Public Trust: An Interactive Artwork
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T173000
UID:6a848355b20478002993b028@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How serious are the promises we make to one another\, the vows
  we take\, or the pledges made by our civic leaders?\nPaul Ramírez Jonas
 ’s interactive artwork\,\nPublic Trust\n\, asks participants of all ages
  to examine the value of their word by declaring a promise that is recorde
 d in a drawing they can keep. Each promise is then published on a large-sc
 ale marquee board and placed alongside commitments made by politicians\, s
 cientists\, economists\, companies and weather forecasters—all drawn dai
 ly from headline news.\nDrop in and make your mark. Add your promise to th
 is evolving public artwork and be part of a collective conversation about 
 what it means to give your word.\nPublic Trust\nis presented by The Bentwa
 y in partnership with the Waterfront BIA and in collaboration with Toronto
  Public Library and Harbourfront Centre.\nThis initiative is made possible
  by donations to the Toronto Public Library Foundation and is generously s
 upported by the McConnell Foundation.\n*****\nCheck out\nKnowYourVote.TO\n
 and\nCelebrate Democracy\nto learn more about Toronto’s upcoming municip
 al election\, access important voter resources\, and discover activities a
 nd interactive library programs for all ages happening at a branch near yo
 u.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Branch Atrium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a848355b20478002993b028
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
