DESCRIPTION:Interested in making your own custom stickers? Join us for a h
 ands-on introduction to Cricut machines and Cricut Design Space. In this b
 eginner-friendly class\, you will learn the basics of designing\, printing
 \, and cutting your own stickers from start to finish.\nCreate personalize
 d stickers to decorate your notebook\, water bottle\, laptop\, journal\, o
 r other favourite items. You can also make unique designs to share with fr
 iends and family or use for gifts and crafts. Staff will guide you through
  the process and introduce the tools and techniques needed to bring your i
 deas to life.\nWhat to bring: Please bring the images you would like to tu
 rn into stickers in PNG or JPEG format on a USB drive\, or have them acces
 sible on your phone or email.\nThis is an in-person event. Registration is
  required.\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
