SUMMARY:Artist Talk: Paul Ramírez Jonas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T193000
UID:6a8483fe57c264087ad1f3ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Hear acclaimed artist Paul Ramírez Jonas discuss his imaginat
 ive body of work and his long-standing interest in democracy\, participati
 on and the public realm. Ramírez Jonas will be in conversation with Anna 
 Gallagher-Ross\, The Bentway’s Director of Programming.\nFrom Key to the
  City and The Commons to Public Trust\, Ramírez Jonas’s work invites us
  to think about what it means to participate in—and take responsibility 
 for—the cities and communities we share. The conversation will explore h
 ow everyday acts of exchange\, promise and participation can create opport
 unities to imagine new ways of living together.\nCome early to participate
  in Public Trust\nand add your own promise to the artwork.\nPublic Trust i
 s presented by The Bentway in partnership with the Waterfront BIA and in c
 ollaboration with Toronto Public Library and Harbourfront Centre.\nThis in
 itiative is made possible by donations to the Toronto Public Library Found
 ation and is generously supported by the McConnell Foundation.\n******\nCh
 eck out\nKnowYourVote.TO\nand\nCelebrate Democracy\nto learn more about To
 ronto’s upcoming municipal election\, access important voter resources\,
  and discover activities and interactive library programs for all ages hap
 pening at a branch near you.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Outdoor Terrace
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8483fe57c264087ad1f3ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
