 join us the first day\, followed by an herbalist and traditional beading f
 acilitator from Kehewin First Nation Register.\nThis event is part of the 
 Artists in the Library program.\nSupplies are limited.\nSeptember 16 | 6:0
 0–8:00 PM\nIntroduction to\nbody oil-making\n.\nSeptember 19 | 10:00 AM
 –12:00 PM\nBath bomb-making workshop\nSeptember 23 | 6:00–8:00 PM\nCon
 tinue and complete\nbody oil-making\nIntroduction to\nfelt-making\nSeptemb
 er 26 | 10:00 AM–12:00 PM\nContinue working with\nfelt\nBegin the\nbeadi
 ng workshop\nSeptember 28 | 6:00–8:00 PM\nContinue\nfelting\nContinue th
 e\nbeading workshop\nOctober 3 | 10:00 AM–12:00 PM\nWork on\nfelting and
  beading projects\nOctober 7 | 6:00–8:00 PM\nFeast\nClosing Circle\nCele
 bration and completion of the program
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a886f1b57c264087ad2b35e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
