X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Bloorwestvillagebia": "https://www.bloorwestvillagebia.com/event/30th-annual-ukrainian-festival/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bloorwestvillagebia
X-SOURCE:Bloor West Village BIA
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260920T160000
DTSTAMP:20260909T222732Z
CREATED:20260220T151241Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T222732Z
UID:2690-1789718400-1789920000@www.bloorwestvillagebia.com
SUMMARY:30th Annual Toronto Ukrainian Festival
DESCRIPTION:Experience the Vibrant Ukrainian Spirit at the Bloor West Village Toronto Ukrainian Festival!\n🔹 Musical Performances\n🔹 Culinary Delights\n🔹 Cultural Exhibitions\n🔹 Children’s Activities\n🔹 Community Connections \nCome for the Festival\, Come back for the Village. 💙\nThe Ukrainian Festival brings people together in Bloor West Village—but there’s so much more to discover beyond Festival weekend. Come back to shop\, eat\, explore and support the local businesses that make our Village special. \n\nContact Information: **Please note\, the Festival is organized by a separate third party organization to the Bloor West Village BIA. It has a Board of Directors and a committee of organizers. \n🔗 Check out more info and festival schedule here
URL:https://www.bloorwestvillagebia.com/event/30th-annual-ukrainian-festival/
LOCATION:Bloor West Village\, Bloor Street West and Willard Avenue (South side of the Street)\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6S 1P4\, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.bloorwestvillagebia.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Ukrainian-FEstival.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/birding-with-beni-fall-birding-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T100000
DTSTAMP:20260913T003701
CREATED:20260722T165514Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260722T165526Z
UID:10002006-1789718400-1789725600@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Birding with Beni: Fall Birding
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fall birding nature walk!\nFall migration is well underway! Join TBG Horticulturist and avid birder Sasan Beni for an engaging walk through the gardens and Wilket Creek Ravine\, as you seek out the wildlife that call this place home. Learn how to identify the many different species passing through and how you can help them in their journey.\n \nBring your binoculars for a better view (we will have extras on hand) and a mug/thermos for a warm beverage and post-birding chat.\n \nAs with any wildlife tour\, the spotting of birds and other wildlife is not guaranteed and is not within the control of the tour guide. Please be patient and considerate. The tour will not be rescheduled due to a lack of bird sightings. The tour will only be rescheduled due to inclement weather.\n \nMeet at the TBG main entrance\, just outside the George and Kathy Dembroski Centre for Horticulture.\n \nFriday\, September 18\, 8 to 10 a.m.\nPublic $22\, Members $20 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Sasan Beni\nSasan Beni is a writer turned Horticulturist. He graduated with a diploma in Environmental Landscape Management from Seneca College in King City\, worked for the Toronto Zoo as a seasonal gardener\, and joined TBG in 2020 as a seasonal Horticulturalist. His home is a revolving door of tropical plants. Beni is also passionate about birdwatching and wildlife photography. In the last three years\, he has led many guided birdwatching walks around Toronto and has written several articles for Trellis magazine illustrated with his nature photographs.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAccessibility\nThe walk will be at a leisurely pace throughout\, following designated pathways and trails\, but sometimes covering uneven terrain and steep inclines. Dress appropriately for the weather and walk slowly. Wearing layers is recommended. Closed-toed shoes are required. We will begin promptly. NOTE: This program occurs rain or shine (save for cases of extreme weather); please dress appropriately for the weather.\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/birding-with-beni-fall-birding-2/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/9834645e7e661edda07a98c5639a5e2a.jpg
END:VEVENT
