SUMMARY:User Ed: Misinformation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T123000
UID:6a8320e6bf1aec09082b1fe7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to separate fact from fiction in a world filled 
 with misinformation and disinformation? Join us for an interactive and ent
 ertaining program where we'll dive into the fascinating world of misinform
 ation\, exploring its origins\, impact\, and how to combat it effectively.
 \nThis program is perfect for curious minds of all ages who want to arm th
 emselves with the skills needed to navigate the complex landscape of onlin
 e information responsibly and safely.\nMisinformation is a topic of signif
 icant interest\, prompting numerous questions. This program is designed to
  be interactive\, featuring activities that provide context and tools to h
 elp you navigate fact versus fiction.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nLive or automated closed ca
 ptioning\, sign language interpretation\, intervenor services\, or attenda
 nt services are available upon request. Please submit your request at leas
 t 2 weeks in advance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-events. ​​
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8320e6bf1aec09082b1fe7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
