UID:6a7e03dd4c610f003894b1b2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Award-winning writer\, chef\, and TV personality\, Sang Kim\, 
 teaches participants how to create a classic Korean rice bowl. Participant
 s will learn each component ingredient\, how to properly use a knife to ch
 op and slice\, and create their own sauce.\n(*contains egg\, sesame oil\, 
 sesame seed)\nFor teens.\nRegister on tpl.ca/programs. Registration begins
  1 month before program start date.\n15 participants maximum.\nLive or aut
 omated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, intervenor servi
 ces\, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your
  request at least 2 weeks in advance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-events.\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
  and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how t
 he library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at
 \nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2
 G8.
LOCATION:Jones
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e03dd4c610f003894b1b2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
