SUMMARY:Jordan Tannahill: The Living Realm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T200000
UID:6a85b55ebf1aec09082b9f53@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Acclaimed author and internationally-celebrated playwright Jor
 dan Tannahill joins us to discuss his dreamlike new novel\,\nThe Living Re
 alm\n.\nWhen a British archeologist living in Berlin begins to see his dea
 d lovers in a cruising forest on the city's outskirts\, he spends a summer
  attempting to make sense of the strange occurrences and finds himself ven
 turing deeper into the mystery of the forest. An expansive and lyrical nov
 el\, The Living Realm is an elegy to the ways our lives become entangled w
 ith history\, the natural world\, and those we love.\nIn conversation with
  Anthony Oliveira.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for pu
 rchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nJordan Tannahill\nRead more:\nLivin
 g Realm : A Novel\nThe Listeners\nDayspring\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocati
 on:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Str
 eet)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets
 :\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events t
 o ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend.
  Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating fir
 st come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available for purchase (debit/cr
 edit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibility. If you are
  Deaf or have a disability and would like to request accommodation for thi
 s event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at leas
 t three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nThis event is part of our signatur
 e\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local and international authors\, artist
 s and thinkers in conversation about their new books and big ideas.\n***\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be
  contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b55ebf1aec09082b9f53
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
