SUMMARY:Diaries of Mark Robinson Algonquin Park Ranger 1908-1936
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T150000
UID:6a7dc66e4c610f003894a90f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Gregory Klages presents Algonquin Diaries\, comprising the
  diary entries of Mark Robinson about life in Algonquin Park in the early 
 20th century. For over three decades\, Robinson served as ranger\, acting 
 Park Superintendent\, and officer in the Canadian Expeditionary Force. Thr
 oughout\, he maintained daily diaries in which he recorded his experiences
  of significant social\, political\, cultural and environmental events.\nD
 r. Klages is the author of\nThe Many Deaths of Tom Thompson: Separating Fa
 ct from Fiction\n\, a Writers' Trust of Canada Best Books 2016.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7dc66e4c610f003894a90f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
