X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8db79cdd2f7e31fe2e42f"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Death Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T200000
UID:69e8db79cdd2f7e31fe2e42f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A Death Café is a gathering of people\, often strangers\, who
  will drink tea\, have a snack and discuss death together. The aim is to i
 ncrease the awareness of death with a view to helping people make the most
  of their lives. Discussions will be in small groups with no agenda\, no o
 bjectives and no particular theme. Prepare to hear and tell stories.\nThis
  is not a grief support or counselling session. The facilitator for this D
 eath Café is Sharon Lazenby.\nDrop-in\, but space is limited.
LOCATION:Guildwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8db79cdd2f7e31fe2e42f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981bdd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Quilting Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T200000
UID:6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981bdd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The focus of this program is to make quilts for donation\, usi
 ng fabrics that have been donated to the group for this purpose.\nParticip
 ants meet weekly to share ideas and inspiration while working on quilts. T
 here are no sewing machines at the library so any sewing is done by hand. 
 Most participants also work on quilts using their own sewing machine at ho
 me. Quilts are completed both as individual projects and as group collabor
 ations.\nNew members are welcome\, and will have access to the instruction
 s\, fabrics\, needle and thread required to contribute on-site to the curr
 ent group project.\nRegarding dates: The quilters will not meet when schoo
 l is out. E.g. March break and during the summer (July and August) and dur
 ing December break.
