BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b5f5fa71a30d92946b55"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:The Making of She Holds Up the Stars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T200000
UID:6a85b5f5fa71a30d92946b55@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join award-winning director\, writer\, and choreographer Sandr
 a Laronde for an evening exploring the creative journey behind She Holds U
 p the Stars and its acclaimed stage re-imagination\, recently nominated f
 or eight Dora Mavor Moore Awards.\nThe award-winning creative will discuss
  the multidisciplinary production presented by Red Sky Performance\, a pow
 erful Indigenous story of beauty\, resilience\, and belonging brought to l
 ife through live puppetry\, movement\, live music\, and visual storytelli
 ng.\nHosted by arts and life reporter Aparita Bhandari\, the conversation 
 will offer audiences a rare look inside Laronde’s creative process and a
 rtistic vision\, enhanced by imagery and puppets from the production.\nQ&A
  to follow. Books available for purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nS
 andra Laronde\nAparita Bhandari\nRead more:\nShe Holds up the Stars\n***\n
 This program is produced by Ontario Culture Days in collaboration with Red
  Sky Performance and Toronto Public Library. This program is supported by 
 the City of Toronto.\nOntario Culture Days is a province-wide festival mad
 e possible through the support of its foundational partners\, the Province
  of Ontario and the Ontario Arts Council. We acknowledge the support of th
 e Canada Council for the Arts and the Government of Canada.\n***\nPLAN YOU
 R VISIT:\nLocation:\nConcourse Event Space\, North York Central Library (5
 120 Yonge St)\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\n
 Free registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to e
 nsure that the greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Ti
 ckets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first 
 come\, first served.\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Seri
 es\n\, where we host local and international authors\, artists and thinker
 s in conversation about their new books and big ideas.\nIt is also part of
  our\nIndigenous Heritage series\n\, generously supported by TD Bank Group
 \, through the TD Ready Commitment.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\n
 The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public L
 ibrary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d)
 . The information will only be used for event and program registration\, d
 elivery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief s
 urvey following the program. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416
 -397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b5f5fa71a30d92946b55
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904f7caafa6100295f84fa"}
