BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a83191f3b6c71003e5962b7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Robyn Rennie: A Discussion on Blindness Arts\, Disability Culture 
 and Creative Approaches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T200000
UID:6a83191f3b6c71003e5962b7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Meet\nRobyn Rennie\n\, an artist centering blindness arts\, di
 sability culture\, and creative approaches to audio description and senso
 ry access.\nRennie’s exhibition\, SEEING BEYOND\, previously presented a
 t the Orillia Museum of Art and History\, includes paintings\, each accomp
 anied by a life-size tactile replica and a custom-built audio device. Atte
 ndees who are blind or with low vision are invited to explore the tactile 
 surface while listening to Rennie’s own authored description of the work
 .\nWith the goal of supporting broader uptake across galleries and museums
 \, Rennie has made the device schematics open source and co-developed “A
 rtcessible\,” a QR-based smartphone app for accessing audio description\
 , while continuing to critically examine the economic and material barrier
 s embedded in mainstream tech solutions.\nThis event explores:\nBlindness 
 arts as a generative cultural framework rather than an accommodation model
 \nAudio description as a creative\, interpretive\, and aesthetic practice\
 nThe design and fabrication of tactile replicas and dedicated audio device
 s\nOpen-source access technologies and questions of affordability and infr
 astructure\nFree. Register for a reminder.\nDoors open at 5:30 pm for atte
 ndees to explore paintings. At 6:00 pm\, Rennie will discuss their practic
 e\, the exhibition and devices in use\, and how more public institutions c
 an integrate disability-led technological innovation into their programmin
 g.\nThis program is produced by\nOntario Culture Days\nin collaboration wi
 th\nTangled Art + Disability\nas Producing Partner and Toronto Public Libr
 ary. This program is supported by the City of Toronto.\nOntario Culture Da
 ys is a province-wide festival made possible through the support of its fo
 undational partners\, the Province of Ontario and the Ontario Arts Council
 . We acknowledge the support of the Canada Council for the Arts.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a83191f3b6c71003e5962b7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
