X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Microsoft Reactor Toronto": "https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/315505397/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_microsoft_reactor_toronto
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315505397@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043559Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T130000
SUMMARY:Building APIs Faster with Agentic Development and Azure Cosmos DB
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nFrom REST endpoints to serverless A
 PIs\, coding agents can dramatically speed up backend development. This se
 ssion demonstrates how to use an agent to scaffold APIs\, integrate Azure 
 Cosmos DB SDKs\, implement CRUD operations\, and refine the architecture f
 or real-world use.\n\n- Check out the [CosmosDB Agent Kit](https://aka.ms/
 CosmosDB-agentkit)\n- [Azure Cosmos DB Agent Kit for AI coding assistants]
 (https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/cosmos-db/gen-ai/agent-kit/?wt.mc_id=me
 etup_27410_webpage_reactor)\n\n[This session is a part of a series. Learn 
 more here](https://developer.microsoft.com/reactor/series/S-1678/?wt.mc_id
 =meetup_27410_website_reactor)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3155
 05397/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260701T214318Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260701T214318Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Microsoft Reactor Toronto": "https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/316018829/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_microsoft_reactor_toronto
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_316018829@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260913T043559Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T130000
SUMMARY:Production Ready: Observability\, Governance and Deployment
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nThe last episode covers what you ne
 ed before any of this runs somewhere real. OpenTelemetry traces and logs s
 how exactly what the agent did on each turn. Purview handles governance an
 d data protection. Evaluation gives us a way to tell whether quality holds
  as the SDK keeps moving.\n\nThen we deploy to Foundry Hosted Agents so th
 e thing runs as a service instead of a console app. We close by walking th
 rough the full refresh-prompt workflow as a maintenance pattern worth stea
 ling.
