DESCRIPTION:Want to learn to sew or would like a refresher on how to use a
  sewing machine? Our introduction to sewing course will cover the basics o
 f threading the machine\, basic stitches and more. We will be creating a s
 mall pouch. All materials will be provided.\nChildren under 13 must be acc
 ompanied by an adult.\nRegistration is required. Registration opens on Sep
 tember 10\n\, 2026 at\n12:30pm\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed aft
 er 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\
 nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public 
 Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d
 ). The information will only be used for event and program registration\, 
 delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your info
 rmation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a876a8b60ccaf01c01fc36e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
