 r Improvisational Writing Club hosted by Spy Collective (Akash Bansal and 
 Margot Fabre). These experimental writing sessions will blend structured w
 ritten exercises with movement\, collage and more\, in order to help explo
 re your creative potential.\nIn these sessions you can expect to learn unc
 onventional techniques for writing stories and poems\, as well as collabor
 ative ways to write and make art. This program is designed to be approacha
 ble by teens of all experience levels: whether you have been writing for a
  long time or always wanted to try it.\nWorkshops will be delivered in Eng
 lish\, but ESL participants are welcome to join. All supplies will be prov
 ided.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists In the Library\nprogram.\nThis p
 rogram is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for 
 teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always avai
 lable. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with
  a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Weston
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a97396cbe148200298bba35
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
