SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Orange Shirt Beading
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T170000
UID:6a67d7be0d65ac360042a54e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Orange Shirt Day and National Day for Truth and Reconciliation
  are observed annually on September 30. In this workshop\, Brianna Patrick
 \, Objiway beading artist\, will explain the significance of Orange Shirt 
 Day and guide participants in the creation of individual Orange Shirt Day 
 pins that raise awareness and recognize the historical and ongoing trauma 
 that Indigenous peoples experience as a result of the residential school s
 ystem. Presenter will be virtual\, but program is in person.\nThis program
  is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens 
 after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available.
  Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYo
 uth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a67d7be0d65ac360042a54e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
