DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T170000
UID:6a91c41369166f088b95992d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Scholarships are accessible to more students than what is comm
 only believed. And here is the most important thing: scholarships can be a
  game changer for a student’s career\, their financial well-being\, and 
 their bank account. Scholarships\, grants\, and bursaries are available fo
 r high school\, college\, and university students\, and you don’t need p
 erfect grades!\nPresented by Chris Grafos from BridgesEDU\, this program w
 ill help empower teens with information to find and win money for postseco
 ndary education.\nThis is a Youth Hub drop-in program for\nteens only\n. N
 o registration required.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth
  Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, whe
 re helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offer
 ed daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find 
 out more.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91c41369166f088b95992d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
