BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a29a42043b41b3d006d582a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:CONCERT: Folk\, Rock\, Pop\, Country\, and Traditional: Jerry and 
 Pete Celebrate Canadian Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T190000
UID:6a29a42043b41b3d006d582a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drawing upon the vast Canadian songbook\, Jerry Newton and Pet
 er Beamish celebrate our rich musical tapestry - from rock to folk\, to po
 p\, country\, and traditional. Experience their harmony singing and spirit
 ed playing of new arrangements of classic and lesser known gems. Learn the
  stories behind the songs as you listen\, sing\, hum\, or clap along and s
 hare special memories of the timeless tunes of Canada.\nNo advance registr
 ation nor free tickets required. All ages welcome.\nThis program is part o
 f Culture Days\, a nation-wide festival celebrating arts\,\nculture\, and 
 creativity from September 18 to October 4\, 2026
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium on the 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a29a42043b41b3d006d582a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
