DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T153000
UID:6aa43e394ea230006f33ae9c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​A beginner-friendly acrylic painting class where no experie
 nce is necessary—just a willingness to have fun and try something new. Y
 ou'll be guided step-by-step through a simple project by a supportive inst
 ructor. Learn the basics of color mixing\, brush techniques\, and composit
 ion\, while creating your own beautiful artwork to take home. All material
 s—including paints\, brushes\, canvases\, and aprons—will be provided 
 by the presenter. Just bring your creativity and a smile!\nSpace is limite
 d. Registration is required.\nIf you identify as a person with a disabili
 ty and require an accessibility accommodation to participate in this progr
 am\, please contact Accessibility Services by email\, accessibleservices@t
 pl.ca\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to make a request. Please contact us
  at least three weeks in advance.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
