BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69aeef0ab0595799c0a1e605"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Innovation Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T200000
UID:69aeef0ab0595799c0a1e605@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Conversation is the source of innovation!\nJoin TPL Innovation
  Council member\nZahra Ebrahim\nfor a series of lively book discussions ab
 out how we can build a better world by getting better at talking with eac
 h other.\nOur September book is\nHow Minds Change\n\, by David McRaney. I
 n the lead-up to municipal elections this October\, we can expect public d
 iscourse to polarize along political lines. How can we have discussions th
 at change people's minds? And should we?\nFrom "Deep Canvassing" efforts t
 o raise support for gay marriage in the U.S. one voter at a time\, to an 
 analysis of how social change happens on a mass scale\, How Minds Change
  takes a fast-paced\, well-researched look at the science of persuasion.\
 nCheck out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Democracy\npag
 e to learn more about Toronto’s upcoming municipal election\, access imp
 ortant voter resources\, and discover activities and interactive library p
 rograms for all ages happening at a branch near you.\nThis event is genero
 usly supported by the McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Junction Triangle\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69aeef0ab0595799c0a1e605
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa45094f9ed2e00384fe7e6"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Wilfred Buck: A film by Lisa Jackson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T200000
UID:6aa45094f9ed2e00384fe7e6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Lisa Jackson’s portrait of Cree Elder Wilfred Buck moves bet
 ween earth and sky\, past and present\, bringing to life ancient teachings
  of Indigenous astronomy and cosmology to tell a story that spans generati
 ons.\nAdapted from Buck’s memoir\,\nI Have Lived Four Lives\n\, the film
  fuses present-day scenes with re-enactments and archival footage of his y
 oung years of displacement and addiction\, and takes us on an inspiring jo
 urney to the space beyond\, and to the spaces between us all.\nThis NFB fi
 lm won the First Nations Award at the Sydney Film Festival (2025) and the 
 Directors' Guild of Canada Canadian Documentary Award at the Calgary Inter
 national Film Festival (2024).
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Auditorium\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa45094f9ed2e00384fe7e6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
