BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre": "https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/10/livestream-viewing-japanese-canadian-monument-opening-ceremony"}
X-SOURCE-ID:jccc
SUMMARY:Livestream Viewing: Japanese Canadian Monument Opening Ceremony
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T170000
UID:d7f7e3ac5b11cca3d5a548e3700b751a@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Announcement for unveiling of the Japanese Canadian Monument *
 Momiji Capacity has been reached\, it is now waitlist only! *JCCC Capacity
  has been reached\, it is now waitlist only! Please join us at the Japanes
 e Canadian Cultural Centre (JCCC) or Momiji Health Care Society (Momiji) o
 n Saturday\, October 3\, 2026 at 3:30pm EST for the live streaming of the 
 opening ceremony of the Japanese Canadian Monument that is taking place in
  Victoria\, British Columbia. A pre-show program will begin at 3:30pm\, an
 d the opening ceremony livestream will begin at 4:00pm. Further informatio
 n per livestream location is outlined below. The Japanese Canadian Monumen
 t lists the names of all Japanese Canadians uprooted in 1942 AND a second 
 set of names of children born after uprooting and up to and including Marc
 h 31\, 1949\, after which freedom to return to the coast was fully granted
 . The monument acknowledges the forced dispossession and internment of the
  community during World War II while celebrating their resilience and impa
 ct on the region. These names and locations engraved on the wall provide a
  stark illustration of a community torn apart by policies that were driven
  by a confluence of race\, economics\, and power. To set them in stone her
 e is to ensure they are never again forgotten or marginalized. Please regi
 ster from the button below to attend the Japanese Canadian Monument openin
 g ceremony livestream: Waitlist Light refreshments will be served\, and a 
 souvenir book will be gifted to all attendees. Please note that capacity w
 ill be limited based on location selected ( choice between JCCC and Momiji
  (both Waitlist Only) ) . Registration will open at 2:00pm EST on August 2
 4\, 2026 and will close at 11:00am EST on September 24\, 2026 or once capa
 city at each location is reached\, whichever comes first. For more informa
 tion\, please refer to https://hcmc.uvic.ca/project/monument/ . For any qu
 estions\, please reach out to jccc@jccc.on.ca . Livestream Event Informati
 on at the JCCC: *JCCC Capacity has been reached\, it is now waitlist only!
  Thank you for joining the JCCC at the monument unveiling livestream on Sa
 turday\, October 3\, 2026! Doors will open at 2:30pm EST on October 3\, 20
 26 for sign in\, and the pre-show program and livestream will begin at 3:3
 0pm EST in Kobayashi Hall. Light refreshments will be served\, and a souve
 nir book will be gifted to all attendees. Please note that the maximum cap
 acity of the livestream event in Kobayashi Hall is 300 guests. Once the re
 gistration form reaches maximum capacity\, a waitlist for 50 guests will b
 e monitored. Registrants will be contacted via email in September to confi
 rm their entrance status (enrolled or waitlist) . Further details will be 
 communicated via email\, e-blast\, and social media in September. The JCCC
  will also be replaying the livestream throughout the evening beginning at
  7:00pm EST on October 3\, 2026 during Nuit Blanche\, as well as during Is
 sei Day on October 4\, 2026. Registration is not required for Nuit Blanche
  livestream viewing on October 3\, 2026. To register for Issei Day\, pleas
 e visit: Issei Day page . A souvenir book will also be gifted to all Issei
  Day attendees on October 4\, 2026. We look forward to seeing you there! L
 ivestream Event Information at Momiji Health Care Society: *Momiji Capacit
 y has been reached\, now waitlist only! Momiji would like to welcome our c
 ommunity to watch the livestream of the monument unveiling in Victoria\, B
 C\, from the comfort of the Yone and Coby Kobayashi Auditorium at Momiji S
 eniors Residence. Momiji will be providing a small\, boxed meal for the fi
 rst 150 community members and 70 tenants registered. Once we hit capacity\
 , a waitlist will be created\, and we will be working with the JCCC to ens
 ure that as many people as possible are able to watch the event. Since the
  event is overlapping with our annual bazaar\, we are inviting attendees t
 o arrive anytime from Noon to 3:00pm and support our annual bazaar before 
 joining the livestream. Further details will be communicated by email and 
 social media in September.\n\nCategories: Community Event
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/10/livestream-viewing-japanese-canadian-
 monument-opening-ceremony
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
