DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft PowerPoint for absolute beg
 inners.\nIn this first session\, you will:\nCreate\, save and run a PowerP
 oint Presentation\nManipulate and re-order slides\nFormat text and images 
 and apply a design style\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able
  to create and run a simple PowerPoint slideshow.\nPrerequisites: Basic ke
 yboarding and mouse skills required\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
