UID:6a9c65f736204e08fbb9d681@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What does civic innovation actually mean and what does it have
  to do with you? This opening session brings the community together to ans
 wer that question. We will introduce the Civix by Design program\, explore
  what civic innovation looks like in real neighbourhoods\, and most import
 antly\, hear from you: what challenges in your community matter most? Your
  input shapes everything that follows.\nThis program is part of TPL's Inno
 vator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to N
 ovember 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by
  technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you
  create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c65f736204e08fbb9d681
