BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-wheel-throwing-combo-beginner-fall-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T163000
DTSTAMP:20260805T182842Z
CREATED:20260805T182842Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T182842Z
UID:146264-1791293400-1795537800@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Beginner)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building and Wheel Throwing Combo (Beginner)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Tuesdays October 6 to November 24\, 2026\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 18+ \nStart by learning the basic techniques of hand building—pinching\, coiling\, and slab building—to create functional and sculptural wares. You’ll also be guided in the fundamentals of creating and finishing pieces on the pottery wheel. This 8-week class is designed for beginners. \nThis class includes a 10kg bag of clay\, and access to glazes and underglazes. Additional bags of clay can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $412\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $485\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    SOLD OUT\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: October 6\, 13\, 20\, 27\, November 3\, 10\, 17\, 24 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Learn to pinch\, coil\, and roll slabs to create functional or sculptural works\, with a focus on cylinders and cups\nWeek 2: Learn the fundamental of throwing a cylinder on the wheel\nWeek 3: Trim your wheel pieces and learn to make attachments such as handles\nWeek 4: Continue to work on hand-building techniques to create bowls and trays; Learn to make a bowl on the wheel\nWeek 5: Review trimming and trim a bowl on the wheel; Continue to hand build or make new pieces on the wheel\nWeek 6: Learn decoration techniques for hand-built and wheel pieces\nWeek 7: Continue works in progress\nWeek 8: Glaze and complete works \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Chloe Begg\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Chloe Begg is an educator and emerging artist living in Toronto/Tkaronto. After receiving an M.Sc. in Sustainable Development and working for five years in the solar industry\, Chloe pivoted to complete a certificate in Ceramic Arts from the Haliburton School of Art and Design in 2022. In early 2024\, Chloe attended the Banff Centre for Arts as an emerging artist in residence. In the summer of 2024 Chloe participated in the City of Toronto’s Public Art Mentorship program\, which will culminate in a six-month installation at the Toronto Sculpture Garden in April 2026 focusing on play and interactivity. In 2025\, Chloe participated in the DesignTO Festival with a solo exhibition\, The Artist Project in Toronto\, and group shows across Ontario. Chloe is currently working with mentors through the Cohorts.Art and FUSION mentorship programs to further work which focuses on connection\, belonging\, and identity. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-wheel-throwing-combo-beginner-fall-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Combo-Intermediate-Fall-2026.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
