SUMMARY:Author Talk with Briony Penn: The Seabird Trials
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T193000
UID:6aa2d860129d8e0031f11e28@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Award-winning writer\, naturalist and environmental activist\,
 \nBriony Penn\n\, will discuss her new book\,\nSeabird Trials: How A Scien
 tist Took Big Oil to Court and Won\n. At a time when scientists are increa
 singly questioned and silenced\, Penn will share stories of resilience and
  restoration both by the seabirds themselves after one of the deadliest oi
 l spills in the Pacific\, and by those entrusted with their protection.\nP
 enn will be in conversation with\nLouise Blight\n\, author of\nWhere the E
 arth Meets the Sky\n:\na Story of Penguins\, People\, and Place in Antarct
 ica.\nLearn how oil spills and climate change have impacted even the wilde
 st\, most remote corners of the earth by the industries that benefit\, and
  the extraordinary lengths people who love the natural world will go to pr
 otect it—against all odds.\nPresented as part of Women's History Month a
 nd Science Literacy Week\, and as part of TPL's environmental program seri
 es\,\nOur Fragile Planet\n\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Librar
 y\, South Chapter.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual event is free to join and 
 will take place on\nZoom\n.\nRegister to receive an email with details on
  how to join the session and to get a link to the recording.\nCaptions wil
 l be available.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Z
 oom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nCommon Murres\, Dave Ledig/USFWS\,
  Public Domain -\nhttps://www.fws.gov/media/comm...\nPlace a hold or borro
 w from Toronto Public Library:\nSeabird Trials: How A Scientist Took Big O
 il to Court and Won\n(Book)\nWhere the Earth Meets the Sky\n(Book)\nWhere 
 the Earth Meets the Sky\n(eBook)\nWhere the Earth Meets the Sky\n(eAudiobo
 ok)\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa2d860129d8e0031f11e28
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
