BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9887195e6fc10d0550f26a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Author Talk with Dr. Kirsten Johnson on Humanitarienne: A Doctor
 ’s Stories from the Conflict Zone
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T110000
UID:6a9887195e6fc10d0550f26a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As a physician and public health specialist\,\nDr. Kirsten Joh
 nson\nhas led missions in conflict zones\, disaster-stricken regions and u
 nderserved communities. In her book\,\nHumanitarienne\n: A Doctor's Storie
 s from the Conflict Zone\n\, she traces how a strict childhood marked by t
 rauma pushed her to seek independence early.\nJoin this 1-hour presentatio
 n where Johnson shares her story as a global health expert working in some
  of the world's most volatile places and how she pushed back on inequities
  embedded in humanitarian systems. If you're drawn to international work\,
  social justice\, or the ways in which people are shaped by—and in turn 
 shape the world around them\, this presentation will inspire you.\nPresent
 ed as part of Women's History Month.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual event is
  free to join and will take place on\nZoom\n.\nRegister to receive an ema
 il with details on how to join the session and to get a link to the record
 ing.\nCaptions will be available.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and pa
 rticipating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nPlace a hold or 
 borrow from Toronto Public Library:\nHumanitarienne\n: A Doctor's Stories 
 from the Conflict Zone\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9887195e6fc10d0550f26a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
