SUMMARY:The Victorian Cult of Mourning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T150000
UID:6a909b912dac6e00372230ef@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​After the death of Prince Albert\, Queen Victoria became kn
 own as “The Widow of Windsor”\, setting the tone for elaborate mournin
 g customs throughout the Empire. Come to learn about hair jewelry\, mutes\
 , crepe veils\, zinc tombstones\, tear bottles\, post mortem photography a
 nd other elements of the Cult of Mourning.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a909b912dac6e00372230ef
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
