BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"City of Toronto Festivals & Events": "daniellecole.ca"}
X-SOURCE-ID:toronto_festivals
SUMMARY:Cowboys and Wallflowers Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T100000
UID:824d515a402d872a52f7458631624467@toronto.ca
DESCRIPTION:Immerse in collages that blend iconic imagery and wit to chall
 enge gender norms and domestic expectations. Despite shifting gender dynam
 ics\, her work highlights ongoing struggles over household roles. Each pie
 ce is meticulously handmade from vintage materials dating 1800s–1970s by
  Danielle Colle. About the Artist Danielle Cole is a Toronto-based artist 
 whose collages\, composed of vintage graphics\, examine domestic roles and
  consumerism. Her work has been exhibited internationally and featured in 
 CBC Arts\, Kolaj Magazine and Toronto Life.
LOCATION:Assembly Hall Gallery\, 1 Colonel Samuel Smith Park Dr\, Etobicok
 e\, ON
URL:daniellecole.ca
X-SOURCE:City of Toronto Festivals & Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd0c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Sanko Speaks: Drop In Thursdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T140000
UID:6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd0c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free\, culturally affirming drop-in program for adults that 
 promotes mental wellness through creative activities\, discussion\, and he
 althy coping strategies. Guided by the concept of Sankofa\, participants e
 xplore connections between past experiences and present wellbeing while bu
 ilding skills for managing stress and supporting mental health. Activities
  vary based on community interests and needs.\nThis program is in collabor
 ation with TAIBU Community Health Centre.
