DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T200000
UID:6aa0693aaafa610029625fc9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:October      7:\nThis workshop will teach participants how to 
 build and thread a      hand loom and begin the process of creating woven 
 textiles.\nOctober      14:\nThis workshop will guide participants through
  some beginner      weaving techniques and we’ll begin ideating around o
 ur woven patches for      the community tapestry.\nOctober      21:\nThis 
 workshop is a self-led weaving session to make space for      participants
  to create their patches for the communal tapestry.\nOctober      28:\nThi
 s workshop is a self-led weaving session to make space for      participan
 ts to finish their patches for the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be
  sewing completed patches to the communal tapestry as they are      comple
 ted.\nDrop-in\, w\norkshop materials will be provided for the first 15 par
 ticipants. We encourage participants to bring yarn\, thread\, and fabrics 
 to contribute to their weavings. We’ll also reflect on and discuss our c
 onnections to weaving\, water\, and our communities.\nThis event is part o
 f the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa0693aaafa610029625fc9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
