SUMMARY:How Canadians are Feeling about Democracy These Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T193000
UID:6a99ae1baafa610029615271@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Trust in democratic institutions is being challenged in Canada
  and around the world. While many Canadians still believe in democratic va
 lues\, more people are worried about political divisions\, lower trust in 
 governments and public institutions\, false information\, and whether poli
 tical systems are meeting people's needs.\nUsing the latest public opinion
  polls\, election research\, and public engagement data\, this panel will 
 explore how Canadians feel about democracy today. Are concerns about democ
 racy shared by many Canadians\, or are they more common in certain groups?
  What is causing changes in political trust and participation? And what ca
 n governments\, community organizations\, educators\, and local communitie
 s do to help strengthen democracy and encourage people to get involved in 
 the future?\nToronto's municipal election takes place on October 26\, 2026
 . Check out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Democracy\npa
 ge to learn more about the upcoming election\, access important voter reso
 urces\, and discover activities and interactive library programs for all a
 ges happening at a branch near you.\nThis initiative is made possible by d
 onations to the Toronto Public Library Foundation and is generously suppor
 ted by the McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99ae1baafa610029615271
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e24aafa61002961b09b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Make Your Own Interactive Story with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T200000
UID:6a9b4e24aafa61002961b09b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could write a story where the reader chooses what 
 happens\, like a branching adventure\, a mystery\, or a game\, and have AI
  build it with you?\nIn this class\, you'll learn "vibe-coding": using an 
 AI coding assistant to build your own interactive story or simple game. Yo
 u'll design the branches\, describe the rules in plain language\, test for
  the tricky edge cases (what if the player picks the weird option?)\, and 
 end up with a single file you can share with anyone. Just a story you want
  to tell. This is the playful sibling of the practical vibe-coding worksho
 p.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be gua
 ranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAbout the AI Tools U
 sed in This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI 
 tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your o
 wn account for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Re
 sident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on 
 using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool 
 prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\n
 Review privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nRev
 iew privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview pr
 ivacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e24aafa61002961b09b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
