BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Ujima Network: Fridays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T130000
UID:6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free group program that explores mental wellness through a c
 ulturally responsive lens grounded in the Black Model of Health and Wellbe
 ing and the principles of Nguzo Saba. Participants build self-awareness\, 
 learn about the impacts of social determinants of health\, and support one
  another through talk circles and group activities.\nFree registration is 
 required\, speak to library staff for assistance.\nThis program is in coll
 aboration with TAIBU Community Health Centre.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a88ef9ed2e00384f513a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
