SUMMARY:Wildlife-friendly Fall Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T150000
UID:6a6a4869f213992f00c7f72b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At this time of year\, many people admire the fall colours but
  also feel the need to rake and dispose of leaves\, cut dead stems\, and r
 emove fallen branches. But what if this tidying up negatively affects our 
 gardens and pollinators? While we may not see the bees and butterflies dur
 ing the fall and winter\, they are still around!\nIn this presentation\, D
 orte Windmuller\, a Butterflyway Ranger of the David Suzuki Foundation\, w
 ill discuss how to maintain and protect wildlife habitat even throughout t
 he colder months\, and how “leave the leaves” can help nature come bac
 k stronger the next season.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Room B1 (located in the basement)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a4869f213992f00c7f72b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2850561e67cd9cb338adb9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Writing Hard Truths: Ethical Issues & Craft Considerations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T153000
UID:6a2850561e67cd9cb338adb9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How do we tell powerful stories that matter? Stories that expl
 ore family secrets\, confront historical injustices or give voice to margi
 nalized experiences while upholding ethical responsibilities and honoring 
 the complexities of truth?\nAuthor Caroline Topperman\n(Your Roots Cast a 
 Shadow)\nwill lead this writers' workshop that delves into the intricate p
 rocess of writing creative nonfiction that tackles challenging subjects\, 
 particularly those related to family\, displacement\, estrangement\, and i
 mmigration.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2850561e67cd9cb338adb9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
