X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a877458b204780029944e6e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Board Games
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T034500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T190000
UID:6a877458b204780029944e6e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop-in casual board game social.\nThis program is part of You
 th Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school an
 d in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutrit
 ious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor cal
 l the branch to find out more.\nIf you identify as a person with a disabil
 ity or as a person who is Deaf\, and require an accessibility accommodatio
 n to participate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Services b
 y email\naccessibleservices@tpl.ca\n\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to ma
 ke a request. Please contact us at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:Flemingdon Park\, 2nd Floor Youthhub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a877458b204780029944e6e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f34c7a821f90037edc7b1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Chronic Pain Self-Management Program (Conducted in Mandarin)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T123000
UID:6a7f34c7a821f90037edc7b1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This 6-week program helps individuals living with chronic pain
  learn skills that can help them better manage their chronic pain symptom
 s as well as their daily lives. Facilitated in partnership with The Neighb
 ourhood Organization and South Riverdale Community Health Centre. This pro
 gram will be conducted in Mandarin. For more information or to register p
 lease contact Sarah at (647) 296-0839.\nThe Neighbourhood Organization is
  solely responsible for the protection of personal information collected t
 hrough the program registration process.
LOCATION:Parliament Street
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f34c7a821f90037edc7b1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696a8e2c6724c63d00ec90d4"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Knit Wits Knitting and Crochet Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T113000
UID:696a8e2c6724c63d00ec90d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Main Street's knitting and crochet club returns! Share your pr
 ojects with other knitters/crocheters\, teach a technique\, learn a techni
 que\, and enjoy great conversation.\nAll level of knitters/crocheters welc
 ome. Bring your own yarn\, needles\, and crochet hooks. We meet on the sec
 ond floor of the library. Drop-in program.
LOCATION:Main Street\, Second Floor - Children's Department
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696a8e2c6724c63d00ec90d4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd0e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Sanko Speaks: Drop In Thursdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T140000
UID:6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd0e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free\, culturally affirming drop-in program for adults that 
 promotes mental wellness through creative activities\, discussion\, and he
 althy coping strategies. Guided by the concept of Sankofa\, participants e
 xplore connections between past experiences and present wellbeing while bu
 ilding skills for managing stress and supporting mental health. Activities
  vary based on community interests and needs.\nThis program is in collabor
 ation with TAIBU Community Health Centre.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1a68d65abe8002a77dd0e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
