SUMMARY:Archaeoastronomy: Stonehenge and All That
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T160000
UID:6a8f555b69166f088b951cda@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Yorkville Library for an Archaeoastronomy Lect
 ure. Archaeoastronomy\nis the interdisciplinary study of how people in th
 e past have understood the phenomena in the sky\, how they used these phen
 omena\, and what role the sky played in their cultures.  Today\, astronomy
  is considered to mean the scientific study of the universe\, but it  cont
 inues to connect\, in so many  other intriguing ways\, with every aspect o
 f cultures\, including myth\, religion\, and the arts.
LOCATION:Yorkville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f555b69166f088b951cda
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
