SUMMARY:Woodside Square Library Relocation and Expansion Consultation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T193000
UID:6aa01e16aafa6100296243a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Public Library is preparing plans to relocate and expa
 nd the Woodside Square branch to a new location within the Woodside Square
  Mall at 1571 Sandhurst Circle.\nThe new branch location will expand to ov
 er 13\,000 square feet\, which is a 38% increase in space.\nFrom July to S
 eptember 2026\, we have connected with the community through consultation 
 sessions\, focus groups\, and community events focused on library spaces\,
  collections\, programs\, and services for all ages.\nJoin us to:\nGet an 
 update on the project\nExplore the early design plans for the Woodside Squ
 are branch\nLearn how community feedback helped shape the plans\nAsk quest
 ions and share your feedback about the designs during the Q&A\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe Personal Information on this form is collection b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.​
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa01e16aafa6100296243a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e391c197d11325d6f21"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Get Things Done with AI: Build Your Own Productivity System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:6a9b4e391c197d11325d6f21@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if your to-do list could check in on you\, notice what's 
 been stuck for weeks\, and offer to help instead of just sitting there?\nI
 n this class\, you'll explore a personal productivity system built around 
 an AI agent and a weekly-review practice. See how the agent loads goals\, 
 counts what actually got done\, flags the items that keep slipping\, and d
 rafts next week's plan. It can support without cheerleading\, asking "Why 
 has this been stuck for three weeks? Here are your options." You'll try it
  yourself with a practice set of goals\, and leave with the plain-text tem
 plates and a clearer map of how an AI might support you\, ready to build y
 our own system at home.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet 
 skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistra
 tion is required and will start September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your
  spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\
 nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activities
  that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not 
 need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are encour
 aged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which inclu
 de best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy sta
 tements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn 
 more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more abou
 t the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about t
 he tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the too
 l\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e391c197d11325d6f21
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
