X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T140000
UID:6aa45de1f9ed2e00384fecc8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a 6-week course designed to build y
 our confidence by introducing new skills slowly.\nIs This Course Right for
  You?\nFor beginners\, with\nvery\nlimited or\nno\ncomputer experience\nWh
 at Will You Learn?\nOctober 1\n: Use the Keyboard and Mouse\nOctober 8\n: 
 Use Google Search and Maps\nOctober 15\n: Word Basics 1 – Write a Simple
  letter and format a Flyer\nOctober 22\n: Excel Basics 1\nOctober 29\n: Pr
 actice and Review\nNovember 5\n: Practice and Review\nFormat: Hands-on wit
 h demonstrations\nWe provide the equipment or you can bring your own lapto
 p.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Daniel G. Hill\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa45de1f9ed2e00384fecc8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa424c0ab7a8e0037c10f99"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Crafting Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T143000
UID:6aa424c0ab7a8e0037c10f99@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a seasoned maker or just getting started\, come
  join our Crafting Circle for a friendly hour of textile and fibre arts. B
 ring your knitting\, crochet\, embroidery\, sewing\, mending\, or other cr
 eative projects\, along with your curiosity and conversation. Enjoy crafti
 ng alongside fellow enthusiasts in a welcoming\, informal environment. All
  skill levels welcome.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Bagshaw room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa424c0ab7a8e0037c10f99
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1893e290cc4e3a7909babc"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T163000
UID:6a1893e290cc4e3a7909babc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca
LOCATION:Cedarbrae - Closed\, Lobby
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1893e290cc4e3a7909babc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
