SUMMARY:AI for School: Responsible Success for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T180000
UID:6a9b4e3d3b6c71003e5de731@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI can help with schoolwork. So why does it feel like walking 
 a tightrope? How do you use it for learning without fooling yourself?\nIn 
 this youth-focused class\, you'll learn to use AI as a tutor\, quiz partne
 r\, and explainer\, not an answer machine. You'll practice the tutor loop 
 using provided examples: starting with what your interests are\, what you 
 want to learn\, how you like to learn\, and what you already understand. W
 e'll also cover academic policies around AI and when AI is the wrong tool 
 entirely.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Compu
 ters are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is requir
 ed and will start September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not
  be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAbout the AI 
 Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agen
 tic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create
  your own account for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow
  the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practi
 ces on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of eac
 h tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the
  tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the to
 ol\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nRe
 view privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e3d3b6c71003e5de731
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
