SUMMARY:Reading Challenge Fall Book Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T193000
UID:69cd76a1dcd22510c03b318b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join library staff in a relaxed setting to discuss your Readin
 g Challenge progress and share recommendations.\nTake part in lively conve
 rsations\, connect with fellow challengers\, enjoy light refreshments\, ma
 ke your own bookmarks\, and more!\nTake this opportunity to share your exp
 erience\, perspectives\, and challenges\, and gain valuable insights and b
 ook ideas from others. Every reader is encouraged to bring titles to recom
 mend for any category. Let's help each other out!\nChallenge yourself to r
 ead widely in 2026—and discover new reads!
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 1st Floor\, Beeton Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd76a1dcd22510c03b318b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
