BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa411dbf9ed2e00384fd1ce"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Horror Classics on Film: Demonlover
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T130000
UID:6aa411dbf9ed2e00384fd1ce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this second instalment of Toronto Public Library's virtual 
 series on Horror Classics on Film\, critic Saffron Maeve and director Pasc
 al Plante discuss Demonlover\, the 2002 French neo-noir thriller film dir
 ected by Olivier Assayas. Exploring the damaging effects of media and mode
 rn desensitization to violence\, the film has gained a cult-following in r
 ecent years.\nAbout this event's guests:\nSaffron Maeve\nis a Toronto-base
 d critic\, film curator\, and researcher. A regular contributor to The Glo
 be and Mail\, her writing has also appeared in numerous publications.\nPas
 cal Plante\nis a Canadian film director and screenwriter from Quebec\, who
 se debut feature film\, Fake Tattoos\, premiered in 2017. His second film\
 , Nadia\, Butterfly\, premiered in 2020 in the official selection of the C
 annes Film Festival. His third feature film\, Red Rooms\, garnered widespr
 ead critical acclaim.\nAdam Nayman\nis a critic\, teacher\, and author\, w
 hose books include critical surveys of the Coen Brothers\, Paul Thomas And
 erson\, and most recently\, in Mind Games\, the filmmaker David Fincher. H
 e is a regular contributor to The Ringer\, a lecturer at the University of
  Toronto's Cinema Studies Institute\, and he has written on film for The N
 ew Yorker and The New York Times.\n***\nImportant information for accessin
 g this live virtual event:\nYou must register for a free ticket via Eventb
 rite to gain access to this event.\nThis event will be presented in a Zoom
  Webinar. Once registered\, you will receive reminder emails from both Zoo
 m and Eventbrite with links and instructions to access your unique Zoom We
 binar link to watch this event.\nAt the time of the event\, you must be si
 gned in to Zoom or Eventbrite with the same email address that you used to
  book your ticket in order to access your unique event link. Unique event 
 links can only be open on one device at a time.\n***\nAccessibility at Tor
 onto Public Library\nWe are committed to making our content accessible to 
 as many Torontonians as possible. Please call or email us if you are Deaf 
 or have a disability and would like to request accommodation to participat
 e in this program. Please let us know as far in advance as possible and we
  will do our best to meet your request. At least three weeks' notice is pr
 eferred. Phone 416-393-7099 or email accessibleservices@tpl.ca\n***\nInfor
 mation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collec
 ted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, section
 s 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event a
 nd program registration\, delivery and evaluation.\nRegistrants may be con
 tacted to fill out a brief survey following the program\n. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa411dbf9ed2e00384fd1ce
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
