UID:6a9b51982dac6e0037243871@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You've got the business idea. Now come the thousand questions:
  who's my customer\, what's the market\, how do I pitch this?\nIn this cla
 ss\, you'll use AI as a research and planning partner for small business. 
 We'll practice together on a sample business\, turning rough ideas into bu
 siness plans\, digging into markets\, drafting customer-discovery question
 s\, and building useful low-maintenance automation. The most valuable thin
 g you'll get is usually a better question to be tested in the real world. 
 Whether you're starting or growing\, you'll leave with an experiment you c
 an run on your own business this week.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboardin
 g and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience requ
 ired.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 P
 M.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of
  the program.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program inclu
 des activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops
 .\nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipa
 nts are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions
 \, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review t
 he privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaud
 e Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nL
 earn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLear
 n more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more
  about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51982dac6e0037243871
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
