SUMMARY:Runnymede Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T193000
UID:6a9ae11be1fb8f13578bdee0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion of Anne Michaels'\nHeld\nWinne
 r of the 2024 Giller Prize\, this novel follows a WWI veteran whose photo
 graphy business captures ghost-like images of the dead as he struggles to 
 reconcile his past.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9ae11be1fb8f13578bdee0
