X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f35bd1b9d9208e0761908"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Iverna Island: Tika's Vision Board Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T193000
UID:6a8f35bd1b9d9208e0761908@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Led by TIKA\, the seven session workshop series builds towar
 d the creation of individual vision boards.  Workshops will include: visi
 oning creative futures\, dream mapping\, vision board creation and reflect
 ions.  The series is designed to support Black and BIPOC youth.  TIKA is
  a multidisciplinary artist\, composer\, speaker\, and cultural futurist w
 hose work explores healing\, identity\, and collective transformation. Ref
 lective arts-based experiences creates accessible spaces for imagination a
 nd personal growth.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Daniel G. Hill\, Quiet Study Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f35bd1b9d9208e0761908
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
