BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa06943aafa610029625fcd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Crochet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T200000
UID:6aa06943aafa610029625fcd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November      4:\nThis workshop will teach participants some b
 asic crochet techniques      like holding the yarn and hook\, chaining\, s
 lip stitching\, and single      crochet stitch.\nNovember      11:\nThis w
 orkshop will build on the crochet techniques learned in the      last work
 shop\, tackling the half double crochet\, double crochet\, and the      tr
 eble crochet stitches.\nNovember      18:\nThis workshop is a self-led cro
 chet session to make space for      participants to create their patches f
 or the communal tapestry. Workshop      materials will be provided for the
  first 15 participants.\nNovember      25:\nThis workshop is a self-led cr
 ochet session to make space for      participants to finish their patches 
 for the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be sewing completed patches t
 o the communal tapestry as they are      completed.\nDrop-in\, w\norkshop 
 materials will be provided for the first 15 participants. We encourage par
 ticipants to bring yarn\, thread\, and fabrics to contribute to their croc
 het patches. We’ll also reflect on and discuss our connections to croche
 t\, air\, and our communities.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists in the 
 Library\nprogram.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa06943aafa610029625fcd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa44dc686d845003115648d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Nuclear Emergency Preparedness Session for Ind
 ividuals and Households
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T190000
UID:6aa44dc686d845003115648d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:While nuclear emergencies are unlikely\, it is important to un
 derstand the risks\, know how to stay informed\, and be prepared to take p
 rotective actions if needed. The Nuclear Emergency Preparedness session is
  aimed at increasing public awareness and household preparedness for nucle
 ar emergencies.\nThis free session facilitated by the\nToronto Emergency M
 anagement Division of the City of Toronto\nwill cover:\nWhy Toronto plans 
 for nuclear emergencies\nWhat nuclear emergency planning zones mean\nHow e
 mergency alerts and official information would be shared\nProtective actio
 ns you may be asked to take\nHow to prepare a household emergency plan and
  kit for your household\nAll are welcome! Free program. Register for a re
 minder. For more information\, please contact Morningside branch at 416-39
 6-8881.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa44dc686d845003115648d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b519baafa61002961b295"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Bring Your Problem: Can AI Help?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T200000
UID:6a9b519baafa61002961b295@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a recurring problem you think AI might help with? 
 A thing you keep doing by hand that feels like it should be easier? Bring 
 it. If you don't have one\, come help your neighbours with theirs.\nIn thi
 s interactive class\, you'll learn a simple seven-step way to think about 
 problems: what's annoying you\, what you've tried\, what AI could actually
  do\, and where it would fail. We'll gather real problems from the room\, 
 sort them into groups\, and map out what's worth solving with AI\, and wha
 t's better solved without it. We'll also talk honestly about what an AI fi
 x costs: your money\, your time\, and sometimes your private information. 
 The problems AI could help with most are often the most personal\, and the
  most personal ones are worth the most care.\nRegistration is required and
  will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be gua
 ranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b519baafa61002961b295
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
