SUMMARY:Death Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T193000
UID:6aa573568cf597003f935461@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A Death Café is a gathering of people\, often strangers\, who
  will drink tea\, have a snack and discuss death together. The aim is to i
 ncrease the awareness of death with a view to helping people make the most
  of their lives. Discussions will be in small groups with no agenda\, no o
 bjectives and no particular theme. Prepare to hear and tell stories. This 
 is not a grief support or counselling session. The facilitator for this De
 ath Café is Nadine Lavoie.\nDeath Cafés are a global movement. To learn 
 more\, visit the Death Café website. Refreshments will be provided.\nSpac
 e is limited\, please register online\, in person or by phone.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa573568cf597003f935461
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c157fbf8ea89c03acfffb"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:LSP: English Conversation Circle (Interacthon)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T193000
UID:6a4c157fbf8ea89c03acfffb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you new to Canada? Join us for our English Conversation Ci
 rcle\; a marathon of interactive recreational\, social and informational a
 ctivities for newcomers and community members!\nInteracthon Themes:\n-Buil
 ding a digital presence\n-Stories of you through poetry\n-Creating a visio
 n board - goal setting\n-Speed-friending\n-Game booths - ring tossing\, ho
 rseshoe\, categories\n-And more!\nWhat's in it for you:\n-Try new activiti
 es\n-Meet new people and new ideas\n-Get your voice heard\n-Connect to the
  community\n-Explore your creativity\n-Let yourself go and have fun!\nTo r
 egister\, contact Claudia at cmontoya@culturelink.ca\nIn partnership with 
 Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada\, CultureLink & Toronto Publ
 ic Library.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c157fbf8ea89c03acfffb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
