SUMMARY:Creating a Landing Page: Tell Your Story and Track Your Customers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6a99bb084995480655ed74ce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You don't need a full website when you're getting started with
  a new business\, one page can get the job done. This session covers what 
 a landing page should contain\, how to attract customers\, and how to info
 rm them about your product. During the session\, we will look at free tool
 s that don't require coding knowledge\, learn how to collect emails\, and 
 learn how to assess if a business page is functioning correctly.\nRegistra
 tion recommended. Drop-ins welcomed until room capacity is full.\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bb084995480655ed74ce
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f43"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T193000
UID:6a6a661db57350d760b31f43@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet online every Thursday evening\,\nSeptember 24 - De
 cember 10\, 6-7:30 PM\n(12 sessions).\nParticipants are expected to commit
  to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekly basis.\nLea
 rners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digital badge\ndown
 load a certificate of completion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f43
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a73846674e3b8b75db7cd7a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Author Talk:  Christine Higdon: Gin\, Turpentine\, Pennyroyal\, Ru
 e
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
UID:6a73846674e3b8b75db7cd7a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Four working-class Vancouver sisters\, still reeling from the 
 impact of World War I and the pandemic that stole their only brother\, are
  scraping by but attempting to make the most of the exciting 1920s. Gin\, 
 Turpentine\, Pennyroyal\, Rue is a love story -- but like all love stories
 \, it's complicated​.\nAuthor Christine Higdon presents a reading\, talk
  and Q&A about her novel\,\nGin\, Turpentine\, Pennyroyal\, Rue​\nInform
 ation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collect
 ed by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections
  20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event an
 d program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the 
 library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\na
 nswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a73846674e3b8b75db7cd7a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
