DESCRIPTION:Using a cellphone is a life skill! Learn about the basics of u
 sing a cell phone in a relaxed\, drop in setting. In this class we will co
 ver all of the different  parts of a basic smart phone\, the operating sys
 tem\, the home page and how to use Wi-Fi and Cellular Data. We will practi
 ce skills such as taking a picture\, scanning a QR code\, and sending a te
 xt.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a948abc69166f088b960aa2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
