BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f47d1386764026a16f688"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Human Connection 101 Workshop for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T120000
UID:6a7f47d1386764026a16f688@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive workshop to learn practical ways to enhance social health\,
  understand the adverse effects of loneliness\, and discover the benefits 
 of building more meaningful connections. Receive a free social health work
 book\, spend time with other participants after the workshops\, and enjoy 
 some light refreshments provided.\nAbout GenWell: Founded in 2016\, GenWel
 l is a registered charity whose mission is to make the world a happier and
  healthier place by educating\, empowering\, and catalyzing forty million 
 Canadians about the importance of their social health.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview\, Auditorium\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f47d1386764026a16f688
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
