X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Crochet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6aa06943aafa610029625fce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November      4:\nThis workshop will teach participants some b
 asic crochet techniques      like holding the yarn and hook\, chaining\, s
 lip stitching\, and single      crochet stitch.\nNovember      11:\nThis w
 orkshop will build on the crochet techniques learned in the      last work
 shop\, tackling the half double crochet\, double crochet\, and the      tr
 eble crochet stitches.\nNovember      18:\nThis workshop is a self-led cro
 chet session to make space for      participants to create their patches f
 or the communal tapestry. Workshop      materials will be provided for the
  first 15 participants.\nNovember      25:\nThis workshop is a self-led cr
 ochet session to make space for      participants to finish their patches 
 for the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be sewing completed patches t
 o the communal tapestry as they are      completed.\nDrop-in\, w\norkshop 
 materials will be provided for the first 15 participants. We encourage par
 ticipants to bring yarn\, thread\, and fabrics to contribute to their croc
 het patches. We’ll also reflect on and discuss our connections to croche
 t\, air\, and our communities.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists in the 
 Library\nprogram.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa06943aafa610029625fce
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Build Your First App with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop\, you'll 
 use an AI coding assistant to build your own small\, useful webpage\, chec
 klist\, or organizer from scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe w
 hat you want\, review the plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bug
 s\, and write documentation so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nP
 rerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are pro
 vided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will 
 start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guarantee
 d after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in
  This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools 
 (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own acc
 ount for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident
 ’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using 
 AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior 
 to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview
  privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview pr
 ivacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy 
 policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
