DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T143000
UID:69a6387a8089f23c675f654e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Share your love of reading at our Wednesday and Thursday Book 
 Clubs! We discuss new books and old favourites in a friendly\, welcoming s
 etting. Ask staff for more details.\nJan 8 - Eleanor Oliphant is Completel
 y Fine by Gail Honeyman\nFeb 12 - Daisy Jones & The Six by Taylor Jenkins
  Reid\nMar 12 - American Dirt by Jeanine Cummins\nApr 10 - The Kiss Quotie
 nt by Helen Hoang\nMay 14 - The Life Cycle of the Common Octopus by Emma K
 night\nJune 11 - Everyone in My Family Has killed Someone by Benjamin Stev
 enson\nJuly 9 - Family Matter by Claire Lynch\nAugust 14 - The Maid's Secr
 et by Nita Prose\nSeptember 10 - The Great Alone by Kristin Hannah\nOctobe
 r 8 - The Briar Club by Kate Quinn\nNovember 12 - The Secret Book of Flora
  Lea by Patti Callahan Henry
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a6387a8089f23c675f654e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
