SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Study Hall
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T190000
UID:6a95c1e72dac6e003722fd3b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Each Monday the Northern District Youth Hub becomes a quieter 
 space for teens to study\, work on projects and request help from staff. G
 rab a snack and work on your homework amongst friends!\nAll teens are welc
 ome! Drop-in\, no registration required.\nThis program is part of Youth Hu
 b service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in 
 the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious 
 snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the
  branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Youth Hub (on the second floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95c1e72dac6e003722fd3b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
