X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bb80b88596143287d9a3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Legal Oversight and Business Registration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T200000
UID:6a99bb80b88596143287d9a3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At some point the business has to become real on paper. This s
 ession will address the decisions that arise when choosing to operate as a
  sole proprietorship\, a partnership or a corporation\, as well as registe
 ring your business name in Ontario\, understanding your obligations around
  HST\, record-keeping and taxes. We'll also cover the protections new owne
 rs most often skip such as basic contracts\, insurance\, and how to protec
 t your business name and brand. You'll leave knowing exactly which steps a
 pply to you and roughly what each one costs. This session is general infor
 mation\, not legal or tax advice.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins welc
 omed until room capacity is full.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bb80b88596143287d9a3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
