SUMMARY:Learning Things You Love with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
UID:6a9c345929a7dd0d67493d38@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Always wanted to learn to cook\, draw\, knit\, fix a bike\, or
  speak another language\, but have trouble sticking to it? What if you had
  a personal AI tutor?\nIn this class\, learn how AI can become your person
 al tutor for something you love\, or something new you want to fall in lov
 e with. A tutor explains things in the way you understand\, asks you quest
 ions\, and helps you choose what to learn next. Learn how to turn your goa
 l into a specific\, doable learning experiment: options not answers\, with
  a practice that survives a bad day. Decide ahead of time how you'll know 
 it's working: revise\, or stop without guilt. You'll leave with a plan you
  actually want to try\, and a sense for what AI should never decide for yo
 u.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAbout the AI Tools Us
 ed in This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI t
 ools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your ow
 n account for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Res
 ident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on u
 sing AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool p
 rior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nR
 eview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview pri
 vacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privac
 y policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy poli
 cy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c345929a7dd0d67493d38
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
