SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Music A
 ppreciation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T153000
UID:695eed5276261f2800631eb2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Due to the closure of Sanderson Library for Branch Repairs Fi
 nding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Music Appreciatio
 n is on pause until reopening.\nCheck branch page for more information\nF
 inding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Music Appreciati
 on will be moving to\nFort York Library\nlocated at :190 Fort York Boulev
 ard\, Toronto\, ON M5V 0E7\nPlease see here for a full schedule\nThis pro
 gram helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn new skills\, and have
  fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us about programs and 
 services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nJoin us and share yo
 ur favourite song of the moment\, or a song that means something to you. D
 iscover new music\, and meet other folks that share your love of music.\nD
 rop-in\, all are welcome.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all pa
 rticipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis progr
 am is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiativ
 e\n.
LOCATION:Sanderson - Closed\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695eed5276261f2800631eb2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085de"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Financial Workshops for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T160000
UID:6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085de@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by John Stapleton from Open Policy Ontario\, learn m
 ore about government programs\, benefits and eligibility criteria for seni
 ors. These sessions are designed for seniors with low income and those who
  advise them.\nThursday Oct 1: What Do Seniors Get?\nLearn about benefits
  for older adults living in Ontario\, including Canada Pension Plan (CPP)\
 , Old Age Security (OAS)\, Guaranteed Income Supplement (GIS)\, and Guaran
 teed Annual Income Supplement (GAINS).\nThursday Oct 15: Understanding the
  Personal Income Tax System.\nWhat is a taxable income and how can tax cre
 dits\, deductions\, entitlements and exemptions help to reduce taxable inc
 ome.\nThursday Oct 29: Protecting Your Retirement Income.\nLearn how to re
 duce claw backs to GIS and GAINS payments if receiving additional income 
 from employment\, a private pension\, or a Registered Retirement Savings P
 lan (RRSP).\nThursday Nov 12: Coming to Canada and Leaving Canada.\nLearn 
 about eligible benefits for those that resided in Canada for fewer than 4
 0 years between the ages of 18 and 65\, or for those planning on emigratin
 g from Canada after retiring.\nThursday Nov 26: Tax Credits and Benefits f
 or Seniors and People with Disabilities.\nLearn about other tax credits an
 d benefits for seniors\, people with disabilities\, and caregivers\, inclu
 ding the disability tax credit\, the Canada caregiver credit\, and the hom
 e accessibility tax credit.\nRegistration not required. Drop-in welcome.
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085de
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
