BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbc6fef89ee1580051092b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Elmbrook Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:69fbc6fef89ee1580051092b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us the last Thursday of each month to discuss that month'
 s title.  Haven't read the book?  Join us anyway to hear what others have 
 to say and meet new people. This is a drop in program.\nJuly 30 -\nMigrant
  Rain Falls in Reverse\nby\nVinh Nguyen\nAugust 27 -\nWhere’d You Go\, B
 ernadette?\nby Maria Semple\nSeptember 24 -\nMinistry of Time\nby\nKaliane
  Bradley\nOctober 29 -\nGreat Believers\nby\nRebecca Makkai\nNovember 26 -
 \nBlack Wolf\nby\nLouise Penny
LOCATION:Elmbrook Park\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fbc6fef89ee1580051092b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f603ae596674bcd583e839"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:North York Central Library Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T201500
UID:69f603ae596674bcd583e839@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop-in on the last Thursday of the month for a lively book di
 scussion led by a librarian!\nRegular Print copies of November's selection
 \,\nThe Lion Women of Tehran\nby Marjan Kamali\, will be available to pick
  up from the first floor reference desk beginning on October 29\, 2026.\nT
 his title is also available in Large Print\, as an eBook\, and as an Audi
 obook on CD.\nUpcoming Titles:\nSeptember 24 - All's Well by Mona Awad\nO
 ctober 29 - Prairie Edge by Conor Kerr\nNovember 26 - The Lion Women of Te
 hran by Marjan Kamali\nJanuary 28 - To Be Announced\nFebruary 25 - Encampm
 ent by Maggie Helwig\nMarch 25 - The Tainted Cup by Robert Jackson Bennett
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f603ae596674bcd583e839
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a4bb0b44674e2601bb7a7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Boba Drink - Bubble Tea Making Workshop for Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6a6a4bb0b44674e2601bb7a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this Hands-on workshop\, participants will learn to prepare
  a classic milk bubble tea*\, explore the core ingredients\, and practice 
 mixing and decorating techniques. A lidded cup and straw will be provided 
 for you to enjoy your boba during the session.\nThis is an in-person progr
 am for Adults (18-65+). Space is limited. Register online or call 416-396-
 3975. Registration opens October 29\, 2026.\nNote: Food products used in t
 his program may contain or may have come into contact with common allergen
 s. (*Contains dairy and caffeine)\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a4bb0b44674e2601bb7a7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
