SUMMARY:Snap Circuits
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T170000
UID:69b1b388db89981d9df9509a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month we will play with electricity and circuitry. Turn o
 n a light\, spin a motor\, activate a speaker and choose from hundreds of 
 different projects\, or try making your own circuits! For ages 6-12.\nRegi
 stration is required. Parent/Caregiver must attend.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Canoe Table\, center of branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1b388db89981d9df9509a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85d95360ccaf01c01f5ccf"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Origami Lotus Flowers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T180000
UID:6a85d95360ccaf01c01f5ccf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a six-part workshop series that creates a space for ex
 ploring belonging and not belonging through conversation and hands-on art-
 making. Guided by reflective questions\, participants engage in practices 
 such as origami with washi\, drawing\, dyeing\, and writing\, using the lo
 tus as a shared symbol of transformation and resilience across cultures. T
 he workshops foster an inclusive\, supportive environment\, particularly f
 or those who feel marginalized or disconnected. The series culminates in a
  collaborative public floral installation in the library\, sharing partici
 pants’ work with the wider community.\nLed by artists "Being~inbetween"\
 nThis event is part of the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram.\nThe workshop
 s are open to youth\, ages 13-17\, and require no prior artistic experienc
 e.\nWorkshop Dates:\nFriday\, September 11th\nFriday\, September 18th\nFri
 day\, October 16th\nFriday\, November 6th\nFriday\, November 27th\nFriday\
 , December 18th
LOCATION:Thorncliffe\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85d95360ccaf01c01f5ccf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
