BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4e8a137d04302f001671bb"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b62"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T130000
UID:6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b62@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nSat
 urday\, October 17\, 2026\, 10 am-12 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery S
 aturday\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, October 24 - December 12\, 2026\, 10
  am-1 pm\n. Registration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto t
 ickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all par
 ticipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis progr
 am is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. G
 erstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \nperson
 al information collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b62
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9489c960ccaf01c02227ad"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T110000
UID:6a9489c960ccaf01c02227ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect matches older adults with a teen volunteer t
 o provide tech help\, under the guidance of library staff. Learn the basic
 s of using computers\, tablets and smartphones and popular websites and so
 ftware.\nIf you're a teen between the ages of 13-17 and would like to lear
 n more about becoming a Seniors E-Connect volunteer\, visit the\nSeniors E
 -Connect Volunteering page\nor contact the branch.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9489c960ccaf01c02227ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
