BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Build Your First App with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T200000
UID:6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop\, you'll 
 use an AI coding assistant to build your own small\, useful webpage\, chec
 klist\, or organizer from scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe w
 hat you want\, review the plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bug
 s\, and write documentation so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nP
 rerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are pro
 vided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will 
 start November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guarante
 ed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAbout the AI Tools Used i
 n This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools
  (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own ac
 count for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Residen
 t’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using
  AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior
  to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nRevie
 w privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview p
 rivacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy
  policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
