DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T200000
UID:6a4eaf9a71ef13620051875c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join a staff-moderated discussion of select nonfiction titles.
  Explore different types of nonfiction\, real-life stories\, biographies/m
 emoirs\, gain new knowledge\, and engage in lively discussions.\nThis mont
 h's featured title is\nLifespan: Why We Age -- and Why We Don't Have to\nb
 y David Sinclair.\nThis program is hosted on\nZoom\n. The Zoom information
  and link will be shared over email.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n[Start with your own unique 
 description of the Book Club and use the 'Title' button to link to the tit
 le being discussed for the month]
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4eaf9a71ef13620051875c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
