X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c337060ccaf01c0238f67"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:AI for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T160000
UID:6a9c337060ccaf01c0238f67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Staying connected with family\, keeping track of appointments\
 , finding programs that interest you. AI can help with everyday things. No
  jargon\, no pressure\, no experience needed.\nIn this class\, you'll lear
 n how AI can help you write a message in your own voice\, turn a spoken th
 ought into a checklist\, plan questions for an appointment\, and find comm
 unity programs. We'll also talk straight about the risks: AI that sounds l
 ike a person deserves caution\, and we'll practice spotting the scams that
  use it. You'll leave with large-print materials\, one personally useful t
 emplate\, and a simple family safety phrase\, all at your own pace.\nPrere
 quisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provide
 d. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will star
 t November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed a
 fter 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in Th
 is Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (li
 sted below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own accoun
 t for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’
 s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.
 \nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to 
 attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview pr
 ivacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy pol
 icy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy
 \nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c337060ccaf01c0238f67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
